        "title": "Split at integers",
        "body": "On $(k-1,k)$ we have $\\lceil x\\rceil=k$ and $\\lfloor x\\rfloor=k-1$, so the integrand is $kx^k-(k-1)$.\n- $k=1$: $\\int_0^1x\\,dx=\\frac12$.\n- $k=2$: $\\int_1^2(2x^2-1)dx=\\frac{14}3-1=\\frac{11}3$.\n- $k=3$: $\\int_2^3(3x^3-2)dx=\\frac{3\\cdot65}4-2=\\frac{187}4$.\n\nSum: $\\frac12+\\frac{11}3+\\frac{187}4=\\frac{611}{12}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{611}{12}$**"
      }
