    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Partial fractions",
        "body": "$(x^2+1)(x^2+4)=x^4+5x^2+4$ and $(x^2+2)(x^2+3)=x^4+5x^2+6$, so the integrand is $1-\\frac2{(x^2+2)(x^2+3)}=1-2\\left(\\frac1{x^2+2}-\\frac1{x^2+3}\\right)$. Integrating, $\\int\\frac{dx}{x^2+a^2}=\\frac1a\\arctan\\frac xa$ gives $x-\\frac2{\\sqrt2}\\arctan\\frac x{\\sqrt2}+\\frac2{\\sqrt3}\\arctan\\frac x{\\sqrt3}$.\n\n**Answer: $x-\\sqrt2\\arctan\\frac x{\\sqrt2}+\\frac2{\\sqrt3}\\arctan\\frac x{\\sqrt3}+C$**"
      }
